.TH "HTMLINPUTELEMENT.LABELS" "3JS" "November 6, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLInputElement.labels \- HTMLInputElement: labels property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]HTMLInputElement.labels\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property
returns a \f[CR]NodeList\f[R] of the \f[CR]<label>\f[R] elements
associated with the \f[CR]<input>\f[R] element.
If the element has the type \f[CR]hidden\f[R], the property returns
\f[CR]null\f[R].
.SH VALUE
A \f[CR]NodeList\f[R], or \f[CR]null\f[R] if the element\(cqs type is
\f[CR]hidden\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]label\f[R] id=\(dqlabel1\(dq for=\(dqtest\(dq>Label 1</\f[B]label\f[R]>
<\f[B]input\f[R] id=\(dqtest\(dq />
<\f[B]label\f[R] id=\(dqlabel2\(dq for=\(dqtest\(dq>Label 2</\f[B]label\f[R]>
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] input = document.getElementById(\(dqtest\(dq);
\f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] label \f[B]of\f[R] input.labels) {
  console.log(label.textContent); \f[I]// \(dqLabel 1\(dq and \(dqLabel 2\(dq\f[R]
}
.EE
